    "growth_rate_source": "judgment: guided 2-3%/yr production growth to 2030 plus modest price inflation on a constant $70 deck. Every trailing CAGR measures the commodity cycle, not the business: FY20 ($42 Brent, COVID) is the 5-yr base, FY22 ($99 Brent) the 3-yr base.",
    "growth_divergence_warning": "Equity CAGR (6-8%) diverges >30% from revenue (-8% 3yr / +15% 5yr) and EPS (-29% 3yr; FY20 EPS negative). Equity growth is inflated by the July-2025 $50.6bn all-stock Hess issuance. None of the historical CAGRs is usable as a forward rate.",
